--- A map begun empty and written a value that can fail holds it, as a
--- variable would: here a parsed int, which grows past 64 bits. The
--- width pass had converted the empty map into one of plain growing
--- ints while the map held values that can fail, and the compiled
--- program declared the plain kind (E0308) — `map[]` is a map of
--- nothing, of the type it is held as (found probing Magpie's as-of
--- join).
fn by_index[t]
    m = map[]
    m['k'] = int[t]
    return m

log[by_index['5']]
log[by_index['x']]
log[by_index['123456789012345678901234567890']]
